---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../../../data/site';

const updated = '5 November 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Card Control privacy policy | Lakshay Kumar"
  description="Privacy policy for Card Control, a personal tool that reads HDFC Bank alert emails and writes them to its owner’s private Google Sheet."
  noindex
>
  <article class="wrap policy">
    <p class="label">Swipe-less · Privacy policy</p>
    <h1>Card Control privacy policy<span class="pop">.</span></h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <p class="lede">
      Card Control is a personal tool used only by its owner. It reads HDFC Bank alert emails from the owner’s
      Gmail and writes them to the owner’s private Google Sheet. No data is shared with anyone or stored elsewhere.
    </p>

    <h2>Who uses it</h2>
    <p>
      Card Control is built and used by {site.name} for personal expense tracking. It is not offered to the
      public, and nobody else can sign in to it.
    </p>

    <h2>What data it accesses</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Gmail:</strong> read-only access to transaction alert emails sent by HDFC Bank. Other emails are not read.</li>
      <li><strong>Google Sheets:</strong> access to the owner’s own spreadsheet, where it adds a row per transaction (date, amount, merchant, card).</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How the data is used</h2>
    <p>
      The data is used only to record the owner’s card transactions in their own sheet. It is not used for
      advertising, analytics, profiling, or training any AI or machine-learning model.
    </p>

    <h2>Storage and sharing</h2>
    <p>
      Transaction details live only in the owner’s Gmail and Google Sheet. Card Control does not keep its own
      database or copy, and it does not sell, share, or transfer data to any third party.
    </p>

    <h2>Google API Services</h2>
    <p>
      Card Control’s use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
      <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data Policy</a>,
      including the Limited Use requirements.
    </p>

    <h2>Revoking access</h2>
    <p>
      Access can be removed at any time from
      <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">Google Account permissions</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .policy { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem) 4rem; max-width: 46rem; display: grid; gap: 1rem; }
  .policy h1 { font-size: clamp(2.25rem, 7vw, 4.5rem); line-height: 0.95; letter-spacing: -0.04em; font-weight: 900; }
  .policy .meta { opacity: 0.65; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  .policy .lede { margin-block: 1rem 0.5rem; }
  .policy h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  .policy ul { padding-left: 1.25rem; display: grid; gap: 0.5rem; }
  .policy a { text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 0.15em; }
</style>
